From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ronny=20Kr=C3=BCger?=
 <197308427+dangelrk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:06:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the host bas driver: full .b -> Amiga executable pipeline

bin/bas is an AmigaDOS script that shells out to ARexx for all its string
handling and to the ACE BASIC binary utils/parseusing for the #using scan,
so none of it runs on a host.  src/bas/c/bas.c reimplements the driver in
C, keeping the same stages, flags and link lines, and absorbing
parseusing.  Tool paths come from $VBCC/config/ace68k, overridable by
ACE_HOME/ACE_LIB/ACE_INC/ACE_BMAPS/ACE_BIN.

It also translates the AmigaDOS assigns that appear in real sources -
"REM #using ace:submods/list/list.o" is the standard form and every
submodule test uses it - onto the configured host directories.  Without
that no submodule links.

Two bugs in the original are not carried over: it accepted only a single
option token and -S discarded all the others along with itself
(bin/bas:112), and its module test matched an 'm' anywhere in the option
string.  It also works around ace deriving the extension from the FIRST
dot in a filename (lex.c open_files), which turned "my.prog.b" into
"my.prog.b.b" - the pipeline runs on a fixed dot-free name in a temp
directory and restores the real name when copying results back.

Building the whole test corpus exposed one more sign-extension bug that
-Werror=format could not catch, because the casts were explicit:

  factor.c, control.c, declare.c, parse.c emitted 32-bit hashes via
  "%lx" with (unsigned long), which sign-extends a negative LONG on LP64.
  atom, generic_atom, typecase and colon_sep all died in vasm with
  "immediate operand out of range" on #$ffffffffada7caaa.

Since LONG is `int` on the host and `long` on the Amiga, the format
conversions now carry explicit C-type casts - (long) with %ld, (unsigned
long) with %lx - so both compilers agree and neither warns.

Verified on macOS arm64: all 223 non-error cases in verify/tests/cases
build to AmigaOS executables, all 28 errors/ cases are rejected, the 11
yap tests pass, submods/list/test_list links against two submodule
objects into an 82 KB executable, and -S, -m, -Sc, OPTION 2- and dotted
filenames all behave.  make -f Makefile-host amiga-check still builds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
